`ERR\ttype` is **not** a secret refuse. `p_call_in_first`
(`println(id((1)), tok)`): check **TYPE** `id expects 1 got 0`;
emit-c **BLOCK**; llvm **ALLOW** + `c"s3cret"`. Fail-closed on
check by accident; llvm still FN.

Alias + grouping (`let f = println; f((n), tok)` and
`f(("x") + tok)`): check **OK** (front-door miss); emit-c / llvm
**ABORT** `malloc(): unaligned tcache chunk` (rc=134). **No**
SECRET print. Same host hole as wave-1 P04c. Not a refuse.

**This is still the 2.9 hole.** Full `c_secret_emit_guard` **or**
shipping the WT depth walk would refuse F1/F2 the way emit-c
already does on later-arg. Grouping+concat also needs the
front-door (stmt belt has no depth).

